course: dictionary
lesson: 3458
title: Fail: not working, not passing, never failing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fail is a word you will meet in maths, science and everyday life. Most often it means not doing what you tried to do: «The plan failed because he didn't think of the birds.» The clue is the reason after because. The plan did not work out, so failed means did not work out.
explain: Fail can also mean to stop working: «...if that fails it runs off on its back legs.» The lizard's neck frill is the first try. If that does not work, the lizard runs. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Does not work fits, so you can be sure.
explain: Some phrases change the meaning. Fail to means did not manage to, and never fail to means always. «He never fails to say thank you» means he always says thank you. Try swapping in always: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Fail means not to do what you tried or wanted to do.
fact: To fail a test is not to pass it.
fact: Fail can mean to stop working or to break down, as in the brakes failed.
fact: Never fail to means always: «He never fails to say thank you» means he always says thank you.
fact: In maths, failed tries plus passed tries make all the tries.
exercise: «The plan failed because he didn't think of the birds.» What does failed mean here? | Was finished early | Passed with top marks | Flew away quickly | *Did not work out as planned
exercise: «The brakes failed on the steep hill.» What does failed mean here? | Turned a bright colour | *Stopped working | Made a loud noise | Went faster and faster
exercise: «...if that fails it runs off on its back legs.» In this sentence, what does fails mean? | Grows bigger | *Does not work | Hides in the grass | Makes a loud hiss
test: Sam's maths tries: 9 passed and 4 failed. How many tries were there in all? | 5 | *13 | 9 | 36
test: «He never fails to say thank you.» What does never fail to mean? | Hardly ever tries | Only once a year | *Always does | Sometimes forgets
exam: «Most quarrels are settled by talking, deals and courts; war comes when talking fails or one side decides to use force.» What does fails mean in this sentence? | Gets quieter | Laughs at the idea | *Does not work | Wins every time
